---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const skills: [string, string][] = [
  ['Languages', 'Python (primary), C/C++, C#, JavaScript, Lua, Bash, PowerShell, MEL/VEX'],
  ['DCC & CG', 'Houdini (Solaris, HDA/OTL, hython, PDG/TOP), Maya, Nuke, Unreal (Interchange), Blender, Arnold, RenderMan, Deadline'],
  ['Interchange & imaging', 'OpenUSD, MaterialX, OpenPBR, USDZ; OpenImageIO; color management, deep compositing, stereoscopy'],
  ['Cloud & tooling', 'AWS (S3, EC2, Step Functions), FastAPI, CI/CD, pytest, ruff, uv, Rez, Qt/PySide2, Perforce, Git, ShotGrid/ftrack'],
  ['ML / AI', 'LLMs & agents (Claude Code), Stable Diffusion, TensorFlow, PyTorch, Hugging Face'],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Talha Ahmed" description="16+ years building tools, pipelines, and automation for animation, VFX, and games.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    I'm a pipeline &amp; automation engineer and technical artist based in Karachi, working remotely
    and async across timezones. For 16+ years I've built the software that keeps animation, VFX, and
    games productions moving — tools, pipelines, and large-scale automation.
  </p>

  <p>
    My recent work is a core-engineer role at <strong>Epic Games (Quixel)</strong>, building a
    production 3D-asset conversion and automation system on open interchange standards —
    <strong>OpenUSD</strong> and <strong>MaterialX / OpenPBR</strong> — with a Houdini processing
    engine driven from a clean Python API, a pure-Python backend, an independent automated QA gate,
    and corpus-scale batch tooling. Before that: pipeline and TD roles at Blink Industries, Untold
    Studios, One Animation/Moonbug, and Passion Pictures, and a decade at ICE Animations and Post
    Amazers writing tools, plugins, and effects in Python, C++, RenderMan, and MEL.
  </p>

  <p>
    I like the unglamorous parts of a pipeline — the read-the-asset-in stage, the QA gate, the batch
    that has to run unattended over tens of thousands of assets and report numbers you can defend.
    That's what the <a href="/blog">writing</a> is mostly about.
  </p>

  <h2>What I work with</h2>
  <dl class="skills-grid">
    {skills.map(([k, v]) => (<><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></>))}
  </dl>

